```
Reason:
The unconditional addition of 96 to the prefix length fields (`plen_le`, `plen_ge`, `src_plen_le`, `src_plen_ge`) in the `parse_filter` function caused invalid configurations for non-source-specific IPv4 routes. This led to incorrect prefix lengths being set, which prevented the redistribution of these routes.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if(filter->plen_le < 128)
    filter->plen_le += 96;
if(filter->plen_ge > 0)
    filter->plen_ge += 96;
if(filter->src_plen_le < 128)
    filter->src_plen_le += 96;
if(filter->src_plen_ge > 0)
    filter->src_plen_ge += 96;
```
Reason:
The added conditional checks ensure that 96 is only added to the prefix length fields when appropriate, preventing invalid configurations. This allows for correct handling of non-source-specific IPv4 routes, enabling them to be redistributed properly.

